Subject: [PATCH] Reduce Pumpkin template, chunk, and idle pathfinder memory

Loaded structure templates previously retained a block-state description for
every block and a second placement list. Store palette indices, share the first
palette's block array with the placement accessors, and borrow descriptions for
queries. Share immutable block-entity NBT until a placement needs an owned copy.
Update template consumers and cover ordering, multiple palettes, round trips,
entity data, and copy-on-placement behavior.

Retain generation chunks as uniform or indexed sections instead of full-height
dense arrays. Use a dense scratch buffer only during the active noise pass to
avoid per-voxel palette bookkeeping, then compact it before retaining the chunk.
Generation dependencies, dimensions, and block values remain unchanged.

Use packed in-memory palette indices, share light arrays with copy-on-write,
allocate carving-mask words on demand, and grow pathfinding heaps only when
needed. Preserve block values, lighting initialization, and search behavior.

Base-commit: b5b9b9d7010e793806a83c495af223c67e1d35ee

